This directory illustrates Z-matrices with Cl, Br and I
including X sites (a partially positive point charge) on the
C-X axis. This allows representation of halogen bonds.

Z-matrices:
benzclX.z          chlorobenzene
benzbrX.z          bromobenzene
benziX.z           iodobenzene
clbace.z           PhCl - acetone complex
clbacePlanar.z     " constrained to be co-planar
brbace.z           PhBr - acetone complex
ibace.z            PhI  - acetone complex
clbcl.z            PhCl - chloride ion complex
clbi.z             PhCl - iodide ion complex
me2co.z            acetone

Interactions Energies                                      MP2*  MP2*
Complex        E(complex) E(PhX)  E(acetone) r(XO) deltaE deltaE r(XO)
PhCl-acetone    -7.42     4.40    -9.99      3.28  -1.83  -1.30  3.16
PhBr-acetone    -8.29     4.14    -9.99      3.21  -2.44  -2.23  3.13
PhI -acetone    -9.20     4.18    -9.99      3.23  -3.39  -3.22  3.14

* Riley et al., J Mol Model 2011, 17, 3309-3318.

The SOSaq and SOSgas directories have results and example Z-matrices for
converting a halogen with the X site to one without it for chloro-,
bromo-, and iodobenzene.

Note: one can obtain the CM1A charges for Z-matrices with the X sites
via, e.g.,
xAM1SP benzclX or xZCM1A benzclX

However, one should not do QM optimizations or QM/MM calculations
on Z-matrices that include the X sites. The X sites are just for
force field calculations.
